ound [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 2 tsp light [[Cookbook:Molasses|molasses]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|garlic powder]]\n* 2 tsp yellow [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Preheat [[Cookbook:Grill|grill]] to 500–575°F.\n#Combine garlic, smoke powder, and 4 heavy [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinches]] each of salt and freshly ground black pepper. Set aside.\n#Combine remaining ingredients in a mixing bowl. Form into ¾ inch-thick patties and make an indentation in the center of each patty with your thumb.\n#Sprinkle patties on both sides with seasoning mixture. Place on grill and cook, turning often, until desired \"[[Cookbook:Meat and Poultry#Doneness|doneness]]\" is achieved.\n#Serve on buns with cook's choice of cheese and desired toppings.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using ground beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes for hamburgers]]\n[[Category:Grilled recipes]]\n[[Category:United States recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using light molasses]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yellow mustard]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Mesquite BBQ Burger","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 pound ground chuck","sourceText":"1 pound ground chuck","amountText":"1 pound ground chuck","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ tsp mesquite smoke powder","sourceText":"½ tsp mesquite smoke powder","amountText":"½ tsp mesquite smoke powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 tbsp tomato paste","sourceText":"2 tbsp tomato paste","amountText":"2 tbsp tomato paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ tbsp apple cider vinegar","sourceText":"½ tbsp apple cider vinegar","amountText":"½ tbsp apple cider vinegar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Salt","sourceText":"Salt","amountText":"Salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"